WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.640
If you’ve ever taken a vacation to one of
the many islands of Greece, then you’ll

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.440
know why the likes of Crete, Lesbos, and Corfu
are famous for their beautiful beaches.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.200
But there is one beach in particular, tucked
away in a corner of an unknown island that

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.280
you might think twice about visiting.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.280
Why?

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.320
Well, the same reasons that this place happens
to be a site of great interest for the SCP

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.370
Foundation also tend to drive tourists away.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:32.879
Today, we’re talking about SCP-2217, the
strange anomalous happenings that have taken

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:38.039
place there, and how it links to none other
than one of the Foundation’s most infamous

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:39.399
Groups of Interest.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:46.340
At first glance, SCP-2217 is an ordinary,
uninteresting beach, just another pretty,

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.989
picturesque view on a Greek island.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:53.739
It looks like the kind of place that would
be perfect for a romantic walk at sunset.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:55.909
But we wouldn’t recommend it.

00:00:55.909 --> 00:01:00.139
Although you wouldn’t know just from looking
at it, the sand that this beach is composed

00:01:00.139 --> 00:01:03.100
of has some pretty peculiar properties.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.619
It contains the ordinary, non-anomalous things
you’d find in sand anywhere else in the

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:10.930
world, normal levels of silicates and calcium
compounds.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:16.420
But the beach also possesses a high concentration
of cationic metallic particles.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:22.189
These tiny, almost microscopic metal fragments
somehow hold an electrical charge despite

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:23.189
being grounded.

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:28.649
So, it’s a beach with partially metal sand,
nothing too unusual there, right?

00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:29.649
Wrong.

00:01:29.649 --> 00:01:34.469
The metallic particles within the sand seem
to have a profound effect on the natural environment

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:37.700
around SCP-2217.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.310
For one, the metal content of the beach influences
the weather, increasing the number of lighting

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.909
strikes that hit the shore, the metals drawing
the static electricity in the atmosphere.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:53.229
This, along with other weather conditions
and natural processes that take place at SCP-2217,

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:56.610
also have a far more obvious anomalous effect.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:02.600
Lightning, rain, even fish washed up and decaying
on the shoreline have all caused various artificial

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:08.519
structures and devices to rise from the beach,
which have all been designated by the Foundation

00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:13.460
as SCP-2217-1
Among the creations found on the beach in

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:18.260
the wake of lightning strikes are a number
of different forms of machinery.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:24.060
These have included simple clocks and other
timepieces, to complicated automatons.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:29.730
These machines have no notable anomalous properties
as far as the SCP Foundation have found, apart

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:34.680
from the way they came to be; and they are
otherwise fully functional.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.340
Also discovered at SCP-2217 was jewellery,
seeming to be made of discarded waste that

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.000
washed up on the beach in the tide.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.900
Resembling bears and other recurring motifs
of a certain religion, these articles of jewellery

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:53.870
have been made using everything from old lightbulbs,
to hulls of ships and even fish and animal

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:54.870
bones.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.069
Most notably, however, was the appearance
of a city.

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:05.370
Or rather, a model of a city that was created
at the beach and was then referred to as SCP-2217-A1.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:11.830
There is a cliff located on SCP-2217, and
if one is to swim through an underwater entrance,

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.370
they will find themselves inside a grotto.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:19.700
There, somehow carved by tidal erosion of
the rock, is a recreation of an Ancient Greek

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.410
city, although the geographical features of
the model seem to resemble an area near Lake

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.900
Baikal in Southern Siberia.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:31.120
The city bears more of the same religious
iconography to the jewelry that can often

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.319
be found on the beach, but which religion?

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:42.020
The same one that considers SCP-2217 to be
a site of holy importance: The Church of the

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.030
Broken God.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.930
Now, some important context to make note of.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.150
For any who are unaware, The Church of The
Broken God is a religious organization that

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.969
the SCP Foundation has had a number of encounters
with over the years.

00:03:54.969 --> 00:04:00.120
Members of the Church share in the belief
that biological, flesh based life is inherently

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.650
wrong, an abomination, even evil.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:08.990
This religion worships mechanization; the
process of making something, or someone, more

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.830
mechanical in nature.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:16.390
According to the beliefs of the Church, there
were two gods: Yaldabaoth and Mekhane, who

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:18.389
created humanity together.

00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:22.830
Yaldabaoth was the god of flesh and animal
instinct, granting humans bodies.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:27.750
Meanwhile, the god of machine and intellect,
Mekhane, blessed man with the power of free

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.810
thought.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:34.009
As humankind developed its civilizations by
building machines, Yaldabaoth became enraged

00:04:34.009 --> 00:04:37.729
that they were ignoring the instincts she
had bestowed upon them.

00:04:37.729 --> 00:04:42.539
She endeavored to destroy the creations of
man, in an attempt to revert them to the animals

00:04:42.539 --> 00:04:44.910
she had intended them to be.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:50.180
As the Church’s legend goes, Mekhane acted
as humanity’s savior, and tried desperately

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.720
to stop Yaldabaoth.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:57.000
The god of machines shattered himself, transforming
his body into a number of pieces to form a

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.440
cage for his fellow god.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.130
Fragments of Mekhane rained down on planet
Earth.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:06.970
Now, the Church of the Broken God believes
it is their duty to recover these missing

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.880
parts, and put their savior back together.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:14.300
Within the religion of the Church of the Broken
God there exists a splinter faction that broke

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.380
away from the main Church.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:23.850
This group, referred to as the Broken Church,
are the ones that regard SCP-2217 so highly,

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.220
considering it to be a holy site.

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.900
According to a piece of scripture from their
religion, the Broken Church believes the beach

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.030
to be Mekhane’s “workshop.”

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:37.940
The Book of Rites describes the legend of
a boy looking out at the ocean with his family,

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:43.710
and seeing fire rain down on the shore, sent
from God, or Mekhane to the Church.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:49.210
Mekhane apparently proclaimed that the beach
was his workshop, where he “made many wonders.”

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:56.220
“The lightning is my hammer, the Earth my
anvil, the sand my ingot,” Mekhane explained

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:01.260
to the boy, so the legend goes, and invited
the child into his workshop.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.870
The Broken God brought his hammer down on
the boy, but instead of killing him, marked

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:10.009
him as the first of the religion The Broken
Church now follows.

00:06:10.009 --> 00:06:17.100
In 2014, the SCP Foundation recorded an earthquake
taking place at SCP-2217, with the grotto

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.729
containing the model Ancient Greek city at
the epicenter.

00:06:20.729 --> 00:06:25.509
Sending a robotic probe into the grotto to
assess the damage, only to find a surprising

00:06:25.509 --> 00:06:27.460
change that had occurred.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:34.570
For the first time, there were a number of
humanoid figures seen within SCP-2217-A1,

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.830
and worse still, they were under attack.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:43.270
Within the model city, what appeared to be
a number of individuals infected with SCP-610

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:49.130
were ransacking buildings, devouring and infecting
the other humanoid figures.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:54.569
Also known as ‘The Flesh that Hates’,
SCP-610 is a contagious skin disease.

00:06:54.569 --> 00:06:59.479
It is usually transmitted by direct skin to
skin contact, and anyone that is infected

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:06.170
with it suffers a horrific mutation that transforms
them into fleshy, inhuman monstrosities.

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:12.629
These infected creatures will attack and infect
anyone nearby that isn’t also carrying SCP-610.

00:07:12.629 --> 00:07:18.910
Interestingly, the disease was first discovered
to be localized to a small area in Siberia,

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:24.210
not dissimilar to the area that the SCP-2217-A1
model resembled.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:30.160
According to some sources, SCP-610 is “The
Flesh”, described by those following the

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.590
religion of Sarkicism, a cult that worships
flesh and disease.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:40.240
Sarkicism is a sect that directly opposes
and antagonizes the machine-revering Church

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.900
of the Broken God.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:45.800
Three years after the earthquake, members
of the Broken Church staged an attack on the

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.410
beach, hoping to reclaim SCP-2217 for their
religion.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:55.210
At the time, The SCP Foundation had closed
off the area to the public, under the cover

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.639
story that SCP-2217 was private property.

00:07:58.639 --> 00:08:03.160
They had been hoping to predict the lighting
strikes that caused the anomalous devices

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.650
to form on the beach.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:10.060
Instead, the Foundation had to repel the Broken
Church’s attackers any way they could.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:14.699
However, as the lightning began to strike
again, members of Foundation personnel that

00:08:14.699 --> 00:08:20.310
found themselves caught in it seemed to change
sides, all stating that “God needs to be

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.610
reassembled”.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:26.600
Only a year later in 2018, another group of
Broken Church zealots stormed the beach and

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.180
the Foundation outpost located there.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:33.720
This time, the Church seemed to have gained
further reinforcements, specifically members

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.580
of other Groups of Interest.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:40.860
In particular, some belonging to the Church
of Maxwellism and the Cogwork Orthodox Church,

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:45.380
both of which were also splinter groups of
the Church of the Broken God.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:50.470
The Cogwork Orthodox Church arose during the
Industrial Revolution, believing that adding

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:55.490
mechanical parts to their own bodies offered
greater understanding of Mekhane, and brought

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.650
them closer to their god.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:03.070
Maxwellism, in a similar vein, had another
interpretation of the Church’s core beliefs,

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:06.480
favoring smaller, more advanced cybernetic
implants.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:11.290
The Church of Maxwellism sought to modify
their brains to become a collective consciousness

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.590
and commune with Mekhane.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.800
Despite a lot of pre-existing animosity between
the three core splinter groups of the Church,

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:22.360
they were able to successfully capture SCP-2217.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:26.980
The three factions sent a video message to
the Foundation, proclaiming the importance

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.010
of their mission.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:32.910
“Oh, disassemblers who call themselves a
Foundation: what are you a Foundation for?

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:36.730
If you are a Foundation for life, then you
will let us keep this land.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:40.030
For the flesh is coming, and only we can stop
it.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:44.830
We need to bring our God back together immediately,
or else you will all perish…

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.100
And now, it is time.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.380
If you are a Foundation for life, you will
not let this happen.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.700
You will let us defeat the flesh.”

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:57.311
Several more messages were sent to the Foundation,
demanding the release of various SCPs with

00:09:57.311 --> 00:09:59.400
connections to the Broken God.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.850
You see, there could potentially be hundreds
of pieces needed to rebuild Mekhane so he

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:06.900
can lead the Church to glory and defeat Yaldabaoth.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:12.340
A number of these pieces happen to be catalogued
SCPs that the Foundation is either aware of,

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.170
or has in containment.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:22.150
These include SCP-882 or “His Broken Heart”
to the Church, SCP-271, “His Broken Gift”,

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:30.680
SCP-813, “His Broken Eyes”, SCP-1139,
“His Broken Tongue”, SCP-635, “His Broken

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:37.020
Mind”, and finally “His Broken Blood”,
which refers to SCP-217.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:41.230
With the beach under the control of the Church
of the Broken God, any Foundation personnel

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:46.000
left alive on SCP-2217 defected and joined
the Church.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:50.000
In order to retake the beach and re-establish
containment, the Foundation was forced to

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:56.550
do something that they only do in the most
dire of circumstances: Ask for help.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:11:01.860
Together with the Horizon Initiative and Global
Occult Coalition, the SCP Foundation established

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:05.420
what it called The Triumvirate, a joint task
force.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:08.860
In 2019, another earthquake was detected.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:14.210
This time in Lake Baikal, Siberia, where SCP-610
was contained.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:18.550
Not long after, infected individuals were
reported to be attacking Foundation forces

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:21.350
in the area, causing heavy casualties.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:24.450
But then an unlikely event took place.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:29.740
Members of the Church of the Broken God appeared,
their bodies augmented with machinery.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:34.930
These zealots that had fought the Foundation
for control of SCP-2217, were now coming to

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:38.210
its aid to repel SCP-610.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:43.990
According to them, God, or rather Mekhane,
had told them to come to assist The Foundation.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:50.060
Using a large-scale electrical discharge,
instances of the SCP-610 contagion were eradicated,

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:56.990
but this discharge seemed to have originated
from the same island where SCP-2217 was found.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:12:01.420
Following this incident, Robert Bumaro, the
leader of the Broken Church, sent a video

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:06.120
message to the leaders of the Triumvirate,
including the O5 Council, the Director of

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:10.120
the Global Occult Coalition, and the Horizon
Initiative’s Tribunal.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.870
In his message, Bumaro stated:
“It's not too late, you know.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:15.680
This is our world, as well.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:17.640
We both want the Flesh to end.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.390
And we can help you; we can help each other.

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:21.540
Come to the Anvil.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.470
We will talk, and we can save this world.”

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:30.620
The Church of the Broken God, its splinter
groups uniting to take SCP-2217 for their

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:35.940
religion, were now extending an olive branch
to the Foundation and its allies, all in the

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:38.370
name of protecting the world.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:43.590
Shortly after, the Foundation, Global Occult
Coalition and Horizon Initiative began working

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:49.580
collaboratively with the Church of the Broken
God, to prepare for an XK-Class Scenario.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:55.230
Retaking control of the SCP-2217 beach for
now, the Foundation intends to revoke this

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:59.030
current arrangement after the dangerous scenario
has been averted.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:04.720
But perhaps Mekhane’s workshop will prove
vital in reassembling the Broken God and saving

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:10.110
humanity, should Yaldabaoth ever return to
exact her terrible revenge.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:16.501
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Broken God
- Ouroboros Cycle” and “SCP-5094 - Miss

00:13:16.501 --> 00:13:20.010
J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse” for more technological
SCPs!

